---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import FdeLifecycle from "../components/FdeLifecycle.astro";
import { CHANNELS, REACH_OUT, utm } from "../lib/course";
---

<Base
  title="About | The AI Runtime, FDE Engineering"
  description="The AI Runtime teaches the engineering work between an AI demo and a production system, from the perspective of forward-deployed engineering."
  pageSlug="about"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="section measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>
      <h1>Between the demo and production</h1>

      <p>
        The AI Runtime teaches the engineering work between an AI demo and a production
        system. That gap is not model knowledge. It is what happens when the process dies at
        step nine, when the publish call times out after it already succeeded, when a
        reviewer approves three hours later from their phone, and when an auditor asks for
        the evidence.
      </p>

      <p>
        The curriculum takes the perspective of <strong>forward-deployed engineering</strong>:
        every topic is taught the way an FDE meets it, in order.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <FdeLifecycle />
    </section>

    <section class="section measure">
      <h2>How this works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Free to read and watch.</strong> Every course is complete as written and recorded material.</li>
        <li><strong>Optional open-source implementations.</strong> Reference repos exist for people who want their hands on the system; nothing requires cloning them.</li>
        <li><strong>Optional labs.</strong> Failure Labs break the running system on purpose, for those who want to feel it.</li>
        <li><strong>No account required.</strong> Progress, if you want it, lives in your browser and nowhere else.</li>
        <li><strong>Not a paid LMS.</strong> No paywall, no seat licenses, no completion certificates.</li>
        <li><strong>Curated external resources.</strong> When another source teaches a prerequisite better than we could, we link it and say why, official documentation first.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section quality">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE AIR QUALITY STANDARD</p>
        <h2>What makes an AIR course?</h2>
        <p class="muted">The artifact is the credential. Every flagship course must make its claims inspectable and its failures reproducible.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="standard">
        <li>First-principles explanations</li><li>Real production architecture</li>
        <li>One coherent system, end to end</li><li>Failure timelines</li>
        <li>Runnable implementation</li><li>Reproducible Failure Labs</li>
        <li>Explicit invariants</li><li>Industry architectures</li>
        <li>Primary sources</li><li>Evaluations and known limitations</li>
        <li>Public Field Report</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section measure">
      <h2>Who is behind this</h2>
      <p>
        Written by Kranthi Manchikanti, a solutions architect working on agentic systems in
        regulated and healthcare settings, and the person behind
        <a href={CHANNELS.publication} rel="noopener">The AI Runtime</a>: a publication, a
        Boston meetup, the <a href={CHANNELS.lab} rel="noopener">FDE Lab</a>, and the FDE
        Talks podcast.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything here is public and reproducible on purpose: deterministic fixtures, pinned
        environments, open datasets and evaluators. Claims about reliability are only worth
        something if a stranger can re-run them.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="contact">
        <li><span class="contact__key">EMAIL</span><a href={CHANNELS.email}>info@theairuntime.com</a></li>
        <li><span class="contact__key">LINKEDIN</span><a href={CHANNELS.linkedin} rel="noopener">Kranthi Manchikanti</a></li>
        <li><span class="contact__key">SUBSTACK</span><a href={utm(CHANNELS.substack, "about", "subscribe")} rel="noopener">theairuntime.com</a></li>
        <li><span class="contact__key">PODCAST</span><a href={utm(CHANNELS.podcast, "about", "listen")} rel="noopener">FDE Talks</a></li>
        <li><span class="contact__key">LAB</span><a href={CHANNELS.lab} rel="noopener">lab.theairuntime.com</a></li>
        <li><span class="contact__key">EVENTS</span><a href={CHANNELS.events} rel="noopener">events.theairuntime.com</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="reach">{REACH_OUT}</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .quality { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: 4rem; }
  .standard { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .standard li { margin: 0; padding: .7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: var(--t-meta); }
  .standard li::before { content: "✓"; color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); margin-right: .7rem; }
  .contact { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .contact li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
  }
  .contact__key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    width: 7rem;
    flex: none;
  }
  .reach {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .quality { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } .standard { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
